 **Abstract**

-The problem is that combining groundwater evidence is assumed to reduce
-interpretive non-uniqueness, although lower uncertainty does not prove
-improvement, and connectivity alone does not show what a sheaf adds. The
-objective was to test both claims. The method combined four evidence-
-integration experiments with an independent MODFLOW 6/MODPATH 7 generator, a
-public-pipeline test, a competence-matched sheaf-versus-graph ablation, and a
-fresh-seed robust/hybrid diagnostic. Results showed that chemistry was
-complementary topology evidence; age and hydraulics did not retain a
-multiplicity-corrected ranking gain, although entropy changes, and hydraulics'
-calibration changes, did. Correct topology reduced age error by 0.062--0.164
-years, whereas reversed topology degraded or destabilised inference.
-Carbonate reactions remained unrecovered, and adverse controls reduced
-uncertainty while worsening skill. In 64 locked scalar cases, the affine
-sheaf improved PR-AUC over the identity graph by 0.0854 (95% CI
-0.0666--0.1050), while localising cycle incompatibilities, but differed from
-a stronger edge-local graph by only 0.0097 (-0.0054--0.0248) and had worse
-log loss. In a separately locked 128-case follow-up, a local-first/global-
-fallback hybrid improved PR-AUC over edge-local by 0.0200 (0.0073--0.0324),
-including cycle and noisy/missing gains, and native maps beat a permuted
-control. However, the Brier interval crossed zero, mean log loss was slightly
-worse, and leave-one-edge-out robustification worsened calibration relative
-to the original hybrid. The significance is a bounded contribution:
-non-identity relation modelling, conflict localisation and selective global
-fallback, not general superiority over a competence-matched weighted graph.
+**Purpose.** The problem is that groundwater evidence integration is often
+assumed to reduce interpretive non-uniqueness, although lower uncertainty does
+not prove better inference, and graph-based connectivity prediction does not
+isolate a sheaf layer's contribution. We tested both propositions.
+
+**Design and methods.** Seven linked audits were conducted. M7.3 and the public-pipeline
+audit used an independent MODFLOW 6/MODPATH 7 flow, tracer and nonlinear-
+chemistry generator; M7.4 and M7.5 used a separate scalar
+affine graph generator. Locked tests comprised 12, 6, 64 and 128 cases,
+respectively. A descriptive Northern Ghana audit defined the field-data claim
+boundary. Full M7.4 and M7.5 contrast families were evaluated with
+10,000-resample max-z simultaneous intervals.
+
+**Primary representation result.** M7.4 passed identity-limit nesting
+and the native affine sheaf outperformed the identity graph on PR-AUC (+0.0854,
+simultaneous 95% CI [0.0539, 0.1169]) and the permuted-map control (+0.0909
+[0.0571, 0.1246]). Planted-cycle conflict localisation also improved over the
+edge-local graph (+0.0689 [0.0318, 0.1061]). However, overall PR-AUC versus
+edge-local was +0.0097 [-0.0149, 0.0343], and neither Brier score nor log loss
+improved. M7.4 failed the prespecified complete gate.
+
+**Follow-up result.** In M7.5, development selected a local weight of 1.0, so
+the estimator was local-first/global-fallback. Against edge-local, differences
+were +0.0200 [-0.0055, 0.0454] for PR-AUC, -0.00151 [-0.00691, 0.00389] for
+Brier score and +0.00333 [-0.0102, 0.0168] for log loss. M7.5 failed the
+prespecified complete gate. Native maps nevertheless beat the permuted-map
+control on all three outcomes, and conflict localisation survived
+correction.
+
+**Scope and significance.** In M7.3, chemistry improved the topology-ranking
+outcomes, correct topology reduced age MAE by 0.062--0.164 years, adverse
+controls reduced uncertainty while worsening skill, and carbonate reactions
+were not recovered under either tested indicator panel. These controlled-
+synthetic benchmarks support a conditional representation claim: affine maps
+encode non-identity relations and global compatibility supplies a conflict
+diagnostic and missing-endpoint fallback. They do not establish general
+predictive superiority, field validity, or performance for temporal,
+three-dimensional, vadose-zone, vector-stalk or active-learning capabilities.
